{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1403251-oath-if-true-hearts-and-falling-out-of-love","id":1403251,"title":"Oath if True Hearts and falling out of Love.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-17T10:53:40-07:00","id":1403251,"title":"Oath if True Hearts and falling out of Love.","content":"I feel like there has to be a way to leave the oath without cheating on the others but can't quite wrap my brain on the specifics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T11:58:42-07:00","id":1403264,"title":"","content":"I think you can beak the oath simply by renouncing it. You tell your partner that you no longer love her or him.<br /> <br /> You've still broken the oath, but it isn't cheating. In terms of any appearance signifying the oathbreaking, as an ST I'd somehow show that it isn't an egregious betrayal like cheating is. But you're still breaking your oath.<br /> <br /> An oath is a serious thing, especially in Changeling. It shouldn't be done lightly. While some oaths are clearly taken for temporary purposes, the Oath of Truehearts clearly state &quot;f<span style=\"font-size:13px\">orever thou hast me in thy keeping&quot; and &quot;may we never find fault&quot;. &quot;Forever&quot; is a very long time. And &quot;never&quot; is very definitive. It doesn't have an escape clause.<br /> <br /> Your PC is making a very strong commitment there.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T17:51:49-07:00","id":1403446,"title":"","content":"Thats precisely why in Kithbook: Satyrs there is a version of the Oath with a duration of a year and a day. After that, its up to the changelings to renew their vows for another year, or just call it quits. I think that version would enjoy some popularity, and there should be versions of it that allow for polyamorous relationships.<br /> <br /> Personally, i think that if BOTH oath-takers decided to rescind the Oath because they see the relationship isn't working, the Dreaming could release them from the negative consequences. I'd only consider the Oath broken if it were only one of them deciding to end it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T18:36:28-07:00","id":1403452,"title":"","content":"That's certainly valid and I do fully say that it depends on the tone and preferences of the ST and table but I personally lean towards that the Dreaming would punish them regardless.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming takes its Oaths extremely seriously and a broken path requires the appropriate repentance. I personally feel that it adds greater stakes and dramatic tension to Oaths and a certain fairy tale horror vibe to the Dreaming and it's Oaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}